pr_comments:
I've updated the PR to remove all of the IAsyncResult-based implementations, including for authentication.

Cancellation of read/write operations now works as expected, respecting the CancellationToken; that's the primary benefit here. We also get to remove all of the complicated IAsyncResult code, which is how this PR ends up removing ~1500 lines (and one step closer to removing LazyAsyncResult and friends from the repo).

Perf is generally better as well, though that's just a side benefit, as I don't believe we've ever heard complaints about performance with NegotiateStream, given its relatively small use.  Even so, reading and writing gets faster:
```C#
using BenchmarkDotNet.Attributes;
using BenchmarkDotNet.Running;
using System;
using System.Net;
using System.Net.Security;
using System.Net.Sockets;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

[MemoryDiagnoser]
public class Program
{
    static void Main(string[] args) => BenchmarkSwitcher.FromAssemblies(new[] { typeof(Program).Assembly }).Run(args);

    private NegotiateStream _client;
    private NegotiateStream _server;
    private Memory<byte> _readBuffer = new byte[1];
    private Memory<byte> _writeBuffer = new byte[1];

    [GlobalSetup]
    public void Setup()
    {
        var listener = new Socket(AddressFamily.InterNetwork, SocketType.Stream, ProtocolType.Tcp);
        listener.Bind(new IPEndPoint(IPAddress.Loopback, 0));
        listener.Listen();

        var client = new Socket(AddressFamily.InterNetwork, SocketType.Stream, ProtocolType.Tcp);
        client.Connect(listener.LocalEndPoint);

        var server = listener.Accept();

        _client = new NegotiateStream(new NetworkStream(client, ownsSocket: true));
        _server = new NegotiateStream(new NetworkStream(server, ownsSocket: true));

        Task.WaitAll(_client.AuthenticateAsClientAsync(), _server.AuthenticateAsServerAsync());
    }

    [Benchmark]
    public async Task WriteRead()
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
        {
            await _server.WriteAsync(_writeBuffer);
            await _client.ReadAsync(_readBuffer);
        }
    }
}
```

